<title>GERMANY: ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS WORLD CUP DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS WORLD CUP DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>GARMISCH-PARTENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Luc Alphand won the ninth downhill of the World Cup Alpine skiing season on Saturday when he clocked one minute 54.27 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Italy's Pietro Vitalini was second in 1.54.85 with compatriot Kristian Ghedina third in 1:54.86.</p>
